    "title": "Pluperfect Subjunctive and Complex Conditionals",
    "subtitle": "hubiera + participle, third and mixed conditionals, regret, and alternatives to si",
    "footer": "Spanish Learning Program · B2 · Grammar · Pluperfect subjunctive and conditionals",
    "next": "Next: B2 · PDF 3 — Advanced subjunctive"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "After this PDF you can",
      "bullets": [
        "form the pluperfect subjunctive (hubiera + participle)",
        "make third conditionals (Si hubiera sabido, habría venido) and mixed conditionals",
        "express regret and missed chances (Ojalá hubiera ..., Me habría gustado que ...)",
        "use alternatives to si: de + infinitive, como + subjunctive, a no ser que, salvo que"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "1. Forms: pluperfect subjunctive"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "<b>hubiera</b> (or <b>hubiese</b>) + <b>past participle</b>. The participle never changes."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        3.4,
        3.4,
        3.4,
        3.4,
        3.4
      ],
      "head": [
        "",
        "hablar",
        "comer",
        "vivir",
        "hacer"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo",
          "hubiera hablado",
          "hubiera comido",
          "hubiera vivido",
          "hubiera hecho"
        ],
        [
          "tú",
          "hubieras hablado",
          "hubieras comido",
          "hubieras vivido",
          "hubieras hecho"
        ],
        [
          "él / ella / usted",
          "hubiera hablado",
          "hubiera comido",
          "hubiera vivido",
          "hubiera hecho"
        ],
        [
          "nosotros",
          "hubiéramos hablado",
          "hubiéramos comido",
          "hubiéramos vivido",
          "hubiéramos hecho"
        ],
        [
          "vosotros",
          "hubierais hablado",
          "hubierais comido",
          "hubierais vivido",
          "hubierais hecho"
        ],
        [
          "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
          "hubieran hablado",
          "hubieran comido",
          "hubieran vivido",
          "hubieran hecho"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Irregular participles you need: <b>hecho, dicho, visto, puesto, escrito, vuelto, abierto, roto, muerto, cubierto, resuelto, descubierto</b>. Second form: <i>hubiese hablado, hubieses hablado ...</i> (identical in use)."
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "2. Third conditional: the impossible past"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "For something that did <b>not</b> happen in the past, and its imagined result: <b>si + pluperfect subjunctive</b>, <b>conditional perfect</b> (habría + participle)."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        6.4,
        6.4,
        4.2
      ],
      "head": [
        "Spanish",
        "English",
        "Fact"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Si hubiera estudiado, habría aprobado.",
          "If I had studied, I would have passed.",
          "I did not study."
        ],
        [
          "Si hubieras venido, te lo habría contado.",
          "If you had come, I would have told you.",
          "You did not come."
        ],
        [
          "Si no hubiera llovido, habríamos salido.",
          "If it had not rained, we would have gone out.",
          "It rained."
        ],
        [
          "Si me lo hubieran dicho, lo habría sabido.",
          "If they had told me, I would have known.",
          "Nobody told me."
        ],
        [
          "¿Qué habrías hecho si hubieras ganado?",
          "What would you have done if you had won?",
          "You did not win."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "In the result clause, <b>hubiera + participle</b> is often used instead of <i>habría</i>: <i>Si hubiera estudiado, hubiera aprobado.</i> This is common in speech and correct, but <i>habría</i> is the safe choice for exams.",
        "Never use <i>habría</i> in the <b>si</b> clause: not <i>Si habría estudiado ...</i>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "3. Mixed conditionals"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Mix a <b>past condition</b> with a <b>present result</b>, or a present condition with a past result."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        7.4,
        5.4,
        4.2
      ],
      "head": [
        "Spanish",
